; Anomaly Coop - callback routes (docs\MOD_LAYER.md 2.2), read by the engine (coop_router.cpp) on the first handler a
; script registers: configs\coop_route.ltx, then every configs\coop_route_*.ltx and configs\coop_compat_*.ltx by name
; (the root of configs only). A later file wins for the same key. A mod or a local fix goes into its own
; configs\coop_compat_<mod>.ltx: those are read last, so they win over every coop_route*.ltx, the generated
; coop_route_stock.ltx and coop_route_gamma.ltx included. Not a DLTX mod_coop_route_*.ltx: DLTX merges into this file,
; which is read first, so any key of a later coop_route_*.ltx overrides it (review M1). A rule for a script that is
; not installed changes nothing.
;
; Every handler registered through RegisterScriptCallback, AddUniqueCall or CreateTimeEvent gets a domain once, when it
; is registered (scripts\coop_route.script asks the engine): by the CALLBACK (the engine's table, xrCoop\coop_routes.h:
; actor_* owner, npc_* / monster_* / squad_* host, GUI_* / on_key_* view, save_state host, load_state view, a mod's own
; callback owner; unique calls and time events host, F2-29), unless a rule below says otherwise. Scripts that call
; world functions and have no rule are host by the generated coop_route_stock.ltx / coop_route_gamma.ltx
; (tools\gen_route_world.lua, rulings F2-28 / F2-29).
;   host  - runs only on the host                  owner - runs everywhere: the player's own (its world calls go to
;   view  - runs everywhere (UI, sound, data)              the host through the engine, MOD_LAYER 2.3)
;   none  - runs nowhere while a session is on, the host included (mechanics the engine replaced)
;   level - as host until split levels (F3a)
; Outside a session (single player) every handler runs. On a client a handler runs under pcall: a Lua error is logged
; and counted (coop_status), the session goes on (R-11.4). A skipped unique call stays registered, a skipped time event
; is removed.
;
; Sections, strongest first:
;   [route_pairs]            callback@script = domain   one script on one callback
;   [route_callbacks_forced] callback = domain          beats the script rules, except a script routed to none
;   [route_scripts]          script = domain            the exact name, else the longest prefix (a trailing *)
;   [route_callbacks]        callback = domain          a callback's default, weaker than any script rule
;   [route_none_functions]   module.function            replaced by a "disabled" message on a co-op client
; Script names: a .script by its name without .script; a .lua by its path under gamedata\scripts, folders joined by
; dots (illish\patches\xr_combat_ignore.lua = illish.patches.xr_combat_ignore), so a mod's patch file never takes the
; rules of the stock script it patches. Names compare without letter case.
;
; Migrated from coop_domains.ltx (F2 T10): [view] / [owner] / [host] -> [route_scripts] with that domain; [blocked]
; (debug tools: host but never a client) -> host; [callbacks_always] -> forced view; [callbacks_host] -> forced host;
; [blocked_functions] -> [route_none_functions]. Gone: [settings] default = host (unknown scripts follow the callback,
; review R5 I4), c_functions (an engine function follows the callback too), protect_client_callbacks (always on),
; disable_dev_debug (always on, coop_main.script).

[route_callbacks_forced]
; Run on clients whatever the script's rule: they only read data or adapt the UI (was [callbacks_always]).
load_state                        = view
on_pstor_load_all                 = view
on_xml_read                       = view   ; dxml_core keeps these handlers itself, they never reach axr_main
on_localization_change            = view
on_screen_resolution_changed      = view
; Never run on clients, even for view/owner scripts: ALife / simulation driven, saving (was [callbacks_host]). With
; script rules winning, coop_* = view would otherwise run them on clients.
squad_on_npc_creation             = host
